nk":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T02:28:57-07:00","id":1075413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1074499-persona-5-is-beast-the-primordial-from-the-heroes-perspective?p=1075336#post1075336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how predatory they are and their overall goal to reform criminals by terrorizing them, the Phantom Thieves are much closer to Beasts who fight against other Beasts who have gone far, far off the deep end (or, for a better fit, Beasts who specifically hunt mortals who don't have a major supernatural template, but who have a miscellaneous ability to affect the Temenos or the Primordial Dream).</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans who could be Heroes but still have enough sense of self to not go on the Hunt? They still can effect the Dream because they are connected to it. (They probably are close to dropping into Hero Status but &quot;Something&quot; doesn't allow that to happen.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 04-09-